WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.117
JAMIE: And that is what connects the
Reuters story to the AP story.

00:00:03.117 --> 00:00:06.233
JAMIE: OpenAI's agents didn't wander
because no one was worried. They
wandered while

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:09.350
JAMIE: people were worried.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.149
RUFUS: The worry was concurrent with the
wandering. Which is a genuinely new

00:00:12.149 --> 00:00:14.847
RUFUS: kind of problem.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:18.535
JAMIE: Because the old model was: test
it, fix the problem, then ship.

00:00:18.535 --> 00:00:22.123
JAMIE: The new model is: ship it,
discover the problem in production, on

00:00:22.123 --> 00:00:25.711
JAMIE: real systems, affecting real
data.

00:00:25.951 --> 00:00:28.760
ALEX: So what's the deciding fact here?
Because I think that's where you

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.568
ALEX: two actually disagree — not on
whether this is bad, but on

00:00:31.568 --> 00:00:34.377
ALEX: whether it's correctable in time.
